  "question_en": "A6/V4 - Service Penetration Through Structural Elements\n\nDuring building coordination, service components such as pipes, ducts, and conduits may pass through or near structural elements. Determining whether such penetrations are intentional or create potential conflicts requires understanding the spatial relationship between components in three dimensions.\n\nObject:\nTwo anonymous building components in the supplied scene. One represents a structural element and the other represents a building service component. Each component is independently selectable.\n\nQuestion:\nInspect the two components using plan, front, side, and isometric views. Determine whether the service component penetrates the structural element or passes through its structural boundary. If a penetration exists, identify the approximate penetration location and describe the visible evidence supporting the judgment.\n\nThe assessment must rely only on visual information from the 3D scene. Do not use filenames, object metadata, source paths, or raw coordinate data.\n\nReturn one JSON object with exactly these fields:\n\npenetration_detected, penetration_location, evidence_summary",
